  "[action] eldest son leaves land with wife",
  "[action] Wang Lung watches his sons with a mixture of pride and unease.",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"Well, and I am a man now and I have a wife and we live in a fine house and I am rich and I have my son and I have a fine wife and I have many things and I am not like my father and I am not like my father and I have many things and I am not like my father and I am not like my father and I have many things and I am not like my father and I am not like my father.\"",
  "[action] The second son laughs at his brother's bragging.",
  "[silence] Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "[action] Wang Lung sits and watches, smoking his pipe.",
  "[action] eldest son sits and talks about his son",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and I have my son and he is a fine little fellow and I have many things and I am not like my father and I am not like my father.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"And has he any sons?\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and has he any sons?\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and has he any sons?\"",
  "[says] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son replies that his son has sons.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and does he not?\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and does he not?\"",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung tells his son the story of his father's death.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and my father died, and I did not know it, and I went into a shop in the town to be a clerk and I heard of it through the mouth of a woman and I did not go to see my father.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and his face was like the color of the earth when the rain has washed it and there was a gleam of it in his eyes. And I went down the night and buried him myself.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and I never wept. What is the use of weeping over the dead?\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"It is not like me to weep over any dead man.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the second son): \"Well, and he did not weep at my death either, though it was in the night, and I did not know that I was dead.\""
